{
  "$comment": [
    "Canonical analyte reference table for the Florida Water Quality API.",
    "",
    "This file is the normalization dictionary: every contaminant name that any",
    "upstream source can emit resolves to exactly one `id` here, so a PFOA result",
    "from UCMR 5, a PFOA row in a utility CCR, and a PFOA violation in SDWIS all",
    "land on the same analyte.",
    "",
    "`limits[].authority` and `limits[].citation` exist so a number is never",
    "presented without saying who set it. Regulatory values change; the PFAS",
    "NPDWR in particular has been subject to post-promulgation reconsideration.",
    "Treat this table as a maintained snapshot that must be re-verified against",
    "40 CFR 141 / Florida Administrative Code 62-550 before being relied on for",
    "compliance purposes, and see `limit_review` for the last review date.",
    "",
    "Limit kinds:",
    "  MCL   enforceable Maximum Contaminant Level",
    "  MCLG  non-enforceable public-health goal",
    "  AL    Lead and Copper Rule action level (90th-percentile trigger)",
    "  MRDL  Maximum Residual Disinfectant Level",
    "  MRDLG Maximum Residual Disinfectant Level Goal",
    "  SMCL  secondary (aesthetic) standard, not health-enforceable",
    "  HBWC  Health-Based Water Concentration, used as a PFAS Hazard Index divisor",
    "  TT    treatment technique in lieu of a numeric limit"
  ],
  "version": "2026.08.1",
  "limit_review": {
    "reviewed": "2026-08-15",
    "reviewed_against": "EPA National Primary Drinking Water Regulations; PFAS NPDWR (89 FR 32532, April 2024)",
    "caveat": "The 2024 PFAS NPDWR has been subject to ongoing reconsideration and compliance-date changes. Re-verify PFOA/PFOS/PFHxS/PFNA/HFPO-DA limits and their compliance dates against the current CFR before using them for a compliance determination."
  },
